-- Backfill: the VAULT/INIT and BOND/POSTED rows the indexer skipped.
--
-- Not a migration: one-off data for the live testnet project, applied by hand
-- with the owner's go-ahead. Safe to run more than once (on conflict do nothing).
--
-- Why: a vault's initialize emits both events inside the factory's create_vault
-- transaction, before the vault is in `projects`, which was all the indexer
-- read. Only #1 and #10 kept them, so every other vault's Record tab is missing
-- "The builder locked a deposit in the vault." The indexer now reads a vault
-- deployed inside its scan range (src/lib/indexer-scan.ts).
--
-- Every row was checked against two sources, and matched each exactly:
--   * #8, #9, #11-#22: the RPC's getEvents, and the create_vault transaction
--     meta from stellar.expert's API;
--   * #2-#7, past the RPC's ~7-day retention: the transaction meta from
--     stellar.expert's API only. (Horizon no longer returns result meta.)
-- Rows are marked processed: the handler for these events only re-reads the
-- vault, which later events have done since, and neither one notifies anyone.
--
-- Regenerate (read-only) with:
--   node --env-file=.env.local scripts/backfill-vault-opening-events.mjs

